Z||000000||Jefrysuko||07-17-2001||09:27 PM||||Ok guy's I got an 86 SE over the weekend and I noticed on the test drive that the left turn signal didn't work so I figured that there were some burnt out bulbs.  I checked the bulbs and they appear to be fine so I guess it is in the wiring somewhere.  Here is the deal.<P>The front drivers side turn/parking lamp and the turn/side marker lamp will not light for any reason.  I am having troubles tracing the wiring.  I am wondering if there is some type of conection that goes only to that side of the car.  If I remember right those lights are all on one section of wiring.  I havn't had time to get out the volt meter but then again I am not exactly sure what I would be looking for.  Any help would be appreciated on this one.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jefrysuko||07-17-2001||11:38 PM||||Ok I guess I made some progress the problem is that I don't know how.  I messed around trying to find the wiring again and now the turn signal light comes on in the nose.  The rest are still not working.<P>Something else I noticed is that the left turn signal indicator inside the car comes on when the headlights are turned on.  I am wondering if this would indicate something being shorted out.<P>I am going to check the bulbs again tomorrow to make sure that I have the right one in the nose.<P>Any sudgestions guy's?||||reg||1
